---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		{/* No header bar on the home page: the name in the lead line is the page title. */}
		<main>
			<h1 class="lead">
				I'm <strong>Sean Sobieraj</strong>, a data architect focused on semantic models and knowledge
				graphs for cybersecurity.
			</h1>
			<p class="links">
				<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sobieraj/" rel="me">LinkedIn</a>
				<span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
				<a href="https://github.com/sseancc" rel="me">GitHub</a>
			</p>

			<p>
				Today I'm a Senior Data Architect at the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency
				(CISA), leading data management for its Cybersecurity Division. I defined the agency-wide
				tagging and metadata practices, simplified our enterprise data model from hundreds of classes
				to a handful of domains, and standardized our cyber telemetry on a common open schema.
			</p>
			<p>
				Just as much of the work is cultural: getting teams to build on shared, curated data instead
				of raw feeds, so an analytic written once can run across many sources and be reused by other
				teams.
			</p>
			<p>
				I started out in the U.S. Marine Corps, helping maintain a base network for 35,000 users and
				rising to sergeant. After a B.S. from the Rochester Institute of Technology and an M.S. in
				Information Security from Purdue University on a federal Scholarship for Service, I joined
				US-CERT, where I went on to lead the malware analysis team. I then served as a Duty Officer in
				the White House Situation Room at the National Security Council.
			</p>
			<p>
				Returning to DHS, I designed and built what became CISA's malware triage and reporting
				platform. It cut the time to first findings from days to minutes and stayed in use for more
				than a decade. Later, I led a DevOps team building tools for threat hunting.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.lead {
		font-size: 1.45em;
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.35;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
	}
	.lead strong {
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.links {
		margin: 0 0 2.5em;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.9em;
	}
	.links span {
		margin: 0 0.4em;
	}
	.links a {
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.links a:hover {
		color: var(--accent-hover);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>
